			"date": "2024-03-18T21:15:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mamot.fr/@GoOz\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>GoOz</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Although React is messed up to use for anything these days.</p><p>It made some sense for a SPA where you can pay the relatively big size of the thing, but now it is all about RSC, and NextJS doesn't help with pushing alpha quality stuff for production use where basic things like CSS is not loading for dynamic imports when using App Router which they now recommend despite still not working for everything.</p>",
